# Response headers for Netlify and Cloudflare Pages (both read this file).
#
# Deliberately no Content-Security-Policy: the site loads Google Fonts, inline
# styles from framer-motion, an inline styled map <iframe>, and Lovable's
# cdn.gpteng.co script. A CSP strict enough to be useful would need that list
# audited first — add one once the placeholder content is replaced.
#
# HSTS is intentionally omitted: on Netlify it must be set at the domain level,
# not in _headers, and enabling it by mistake is hard to undo.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=()

# Vite emits content-hashed filenames here, so they are safe to cache forever.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/*.ico
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
